WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back!
-How are you, man?

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm great.
I'm so happy to have you here.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-This movie is very cool

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:07.273
in that it basically -- most
of it takes place on a train.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:10.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
-On a train, yes.
-And yet it's an action movie.

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:11.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And there are many action

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
sequences on the train.
-On the train.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Including -- you have
a fight scene in a train car.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's are many
fight scenes...

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...in said train car.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And what's crazy is there

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:21.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
is only one train car.
-Oh.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's not even a punch line.
Literally,

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:26.559 size:84% position:42%
we shot it on a stage
in Pinewood in England.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:29.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you have to build
a whole train.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:30.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they literally
just did one car

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.800
and then they'd swap everybody
out and put in more background

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:34.801 line:92%
and then shoot the next scene.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know how the director
did it.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:38.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The funny thing is,
no matter how many times

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:40.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
you go on a movie set,
like, I'm sure you thought,

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Great,
I'll be on a whole train."

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:43.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, no.
-They're like, no,

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:44.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's not how movies work.
-One car.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:45.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We're just gonna use one car.
-One car.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:48.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I imagine there is an amazing
amount of choreography

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.384
to a fight scene that takes
place in a closed space.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:52.652 line:92%
-Yeah, it is, definitely.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:56.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one, you don't want to
hurt people.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.158 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:58.158 --> 00:00:59.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because it's also,
like, real seats.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:02.062
And, you know, trains aren't
the most comfortable of spaces.

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.930
-Yeah.
-There's a lot of metal around.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And to shoot it

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:09.502
in such a different way
to make each fight interesting,

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:10.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
is also --
-Right. Of course.

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:13.106 size:84% position:42%
It's like, "Oh, another
train fight, great."

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:13.640 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.475
You've worked with Liam before.
-I have.

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.911 size:84% position:42%
-You were in "A-Team."
-We have fought before.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, you fought in "A-Team."
-Yes.

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:20.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You had a fight
with Liam Neeson?

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yes I did.
-How is he?

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is he one of the guys --
-Large.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's a large man.
He is a large man.

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:27.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
He is surprisingly --
I mean, I know he looks --

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's a giant.
-He's one of those guys

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:31.991
that looks big in movies
and then is somehow even bigger

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:32.592 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in real life.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:33.793 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Yeah, he's like 7'3".

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:34.661 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:35.495 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Yeah, and is he a guy

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
who swaps out for
his stunt double

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.164 line:92%
when it comes time for fights?

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.032 line:92%
-His stunt double is very short.

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:41.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's very --
-It's very hard, yeah.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.570 line:92%
-No, he will -- he'll go for it.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:44.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-In fact,

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:46.406 line:92%
I remember this on "A-Team."

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:49.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
The stunt double usually comes
up after a take and says,

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:51.144
"You know what? You can give it
to him a little more."

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.847
'Cause you don't wanna --
you know, it's Liam Neeson.

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:55.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I know he does this
a lot, but you know,

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
you respect the guy.
-Sure, of course.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You don't want to
sort of go at it.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the stunt double
comes up and says,

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:00.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Give it to him."
-Oh, wow.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he can take it.
-All right.

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well I mean, I believe
he can take it.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would be more worried
about you.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.659 line:92%
Don't take it the wrong way.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.428 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:10.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have another --
-I gotta go.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:12.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm assuming there's plenty
of stunts in --

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're doing "Aquaman."
-I am.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You filmed "Aquaman"
for six months.

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Another large man.
-Another large man.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, that's even --
Jason Momoa.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:21.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yes.
-He must be 7'5".

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:23.143 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-He is, he's like 8'2".

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:24.144 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:25.411 size:78% position:39%
-Because it's great,
because when those --

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you watch the movie,
you're like,

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:27.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I wonder who is going to
win the fight,

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:29.949 line:92%
Jason Momoa or Patrick Wilson?"

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughs ]
-What?

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:32.619 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:34.020 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You're killing me.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.256 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-You play -- Tell me --

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:39.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, I --
You'd beat me in a fight.

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:39.893 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:45.098
You play Aquaman's half-brother.
-Yes. The smaller, shorter...

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:46.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Orm.
-...whiter half.

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:47.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your name is Orm?
-My name is Orm.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-I'm a badass in that movie.

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, no.
-He's the Ocean Master.

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:53.673 size:84% position:42%
-Orm sounds like a guy
you would be scared by.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:54.674 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.676 line:92%
"Guys, look out, Orm is coming!"

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, guys!
You know what's funny?

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.580 size:88% position:44%
You know what's funny?
We would, on my chair --

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.814
'cause the chair in the
movie -- I don't know why

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm referring to the chair.
But it would say "Orm."

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we'd put tape
so it says "Norm."

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.253 line:92%
Which made me even less --

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:11.391
-When you go under water,
you would drop the "N."

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:12.725 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right.

